#15701
A Bright Meadow~
The meadow, once brightened with the splendor of light, golden wheat,
and wild flowers, glistens with the winter’s first snowfall.  Beneath
your warm armor and cloaks of fur, you feel an ominous chill run up
your spine.  Out of the corner of your eye, you see a man, shivering 
and begging you to leave. Although it is difficult to discern his 
maddening words, you swear he repeats, "There can be no good without 
evil, no love without hate, no heaven without hell, no light 
without darkness."
~
